---
type: journal
title: Alibaba token-plan 503 relay and the missing upstream attempt log
timestamp: 2026-10-19
---

# Reported

User, 2026-10-19: using the Alibaba token plan, Codex shows
`503 Service Unavailable` with `Master scheduling failed ...` and argued this is
a ciel-runtime problem rather than a CielAiRouter problem.

# Confirmed observations

- Codex client log (`~/.codex/logs_2.sqlite`) records the response exactly:
  `POST http://127.0.0.1:9489/v1/responses`, `503 Service Unavailable`,
  `server: ciel-runtime/0.1 Python/3.14.2`, `content-type: text/event-stream`.
  Bodies: `Master scheduling failed (INTERNAL)` at 19:29:12 and
  `(UNAVAILABLE)` at 20:02:16 (local).
- The body's `type: ServiceUnavailable` and the message are Alibaba DashScope's;
  no such string exists in the runtime source.
- The requests go to `https://token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com`
  (alitoken), not to CielAiRouter.
- Same router log, same minutes: no `POST /v1/responses provider=...` DEBUG line
  and no `upstream_stream_request` line for the failing requests, while normal
  requests log both. Log level is DEBUG.
- Large requests to the same endpoint/model succeed: 277,169 tokens / 1.1 MB at
  19:27:50 and 241,436 tokens at 20:01:28 both returned 200.
- The provider's saved `custom_models` lists `deepseek-v4.1-flash` but not the
  selected `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`; the model-registry cache does list the
  snapshot, so the token plan advertises it.

# What this establishes

The 503 originates upstream and the runtime relays it. The runtime cannot be
excluded as the cause of that upstream rejection because it recorded no
upstream attempt for the request, which is a runtime observability defect.

# Changes made

- Every `/v1/responses` request logs `responses_request_received` on entry,
  before any route branch, so a request is recorded even when it fails before
  the translated-path DEBUG line.
- Every upstream failure relayed to the client (HTTPError, UpstreamFailure,
  transport failure) logs `responses_upstream_error` with path, provider,
  model, status, error type and a 300-character message. Covered branches:
  translated path, Codex route, native provider Responses route.
- `alitoken_deepseek_v41_flash_1017_20261019` keeps the selected snapshot in the
  saved catalog.

# Not established

- Whether the rejected request was too large, wrongly shaped, or hit an Alibaba
  serving-capacity failure. The new log line answers this on the next
  occurrence.
- The upstream error type's exact meaning; no public documentation found for
  "Master scheduling failed".